# FreightFlow Project Conventions

## Python (Backend — src/api/)

- Use Pydantic v2 BaseModel for all request/response types
- Flask Blueprints for route organization, one Blueprint per resource
- Service layer pattern: routes → services → Supabase/AI clients
- All routes return JSON via `jsonify()`, never `render_template()`
- Prefix all API routes with `/api/`
- Use type hints on all function signatures
- Naming: `snake_case` for functions, variables, files; `PascalCase` for classes

## TypeScript (Frontend — frontend/)

- Next.js App Router: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`
- Use `"use client"` only when needed (interactivity, hooks)
- shadcn/ui as component base; extend with Tailwind utilities
- All types in `frontend/src/lib/types.ts`
- Use Supabase JS client for auth and direct reads; Flask API for pipeline operations

## Database (Supabase)

- `snake_case` for table and column names
- UUID primary keys everywhere (never integer counters)
- `org_id` on every tenant-scoped table
- `created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()` and `updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()` on all tables
- RLS enabled on all tenant tables
- Migrations numbered sequentially in `supabase/migrations/`

## General

- No hardcoded company data (no "Hanson Chemicals" references in new code)
- No global API keys in production paths — use per-org BYOK from `org_api_keys`
- No `session` state — API is stateless with JWT auth
- Document non-obvious logic; don't comment the obvious
